  "Question": "In the circle circumference formula \\(C=2\\pi r\\), which quantities are variables and which are constants?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(C\\) and \\(r\\) are variables; \\(2\\pi\\) is a constant",
    "B": "\\(C\\), \\(r\\), and \\(\\pi\\) are all variables",
    "C": "\\(r\\) is a variable; \\(C\\) and \\(2\\pi\\) are constants",
    "D": "\\(C\\) is a variable; \\(r\\) and \\(2\\pi\\) are constants"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "As the radius \\(r\\) changes, the circumference \\(C\\) changes with it, so both are variables. The value of \\(2\\pi\\) remains unchanged, so it is a constant.",
